# Everything here is copied into the build context before Docker starts, so
# leaving large or irrelevant files out makes every build faster -- and keeps
# them out of the published image.
#
# What must NOT be excluded: data/*.csv (the server reads them at startup),
# data/chunks.json (the question box searches it), and static/ (the page).

.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore

# Secrets never enter an image. On Render the key comes from the dashboard;
# locally it comes from .env on the host. Baking one into a layer would ship
# it to anyone who pulls the image.
.env
.env.*

# 86 MB of NSE files. build.py needs them; the server never opens one.
data/raw/

# The source PDFs. rag.py already turned them into data/chunks.json, which is
# all the running site needs.
docs/

# Verification tooling, not runtime. The C++ solver exists to check the
# Python one, and that check happens in CI.
cpp/
bench.py
tests/

# Write-ups and their sources.
*.pdf
*.md
code-guide.html
explainer.html
summary.html

# Local Python clutter.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
